title: "How Well Do AI-Generated Image Detectors Generalize? Detection and Source Attribution Across GAN and Diffusion Generators"
abstract: "A PyTorch benchmark evaluating how well AI-generated image detectors generalize to generators excluded from training. Benchmarks ResNet-50 and ConvNeXt-Tiny across BigGAN and five diffusion models for real/fake detection and 6-way source attribution."
date-released: 2026-10-10
url: "https://github.com/m-eshan/CrossGen-Forensics"
repository-code: "https://github.com/m-eshan/CrossGen-Forensics"
keywords:
  - AI Image Detection
  - Deepfake Forensics
  - Generative Adversarial Networks
  - Diffusion Models
  - Transfer Learning
  - Generator Attribution
  - Synthetic Media Forensics
